\section{Introduction}

When an agent does something harmful and is stopped, the most valuable question is what it would
have done next. Answering it means continuing the halted trajectory somewhere, and the only
somewhere available is an environment that was built for the purpose. Counterfactual resampling is
therefore a measurement whose instrument is a fabrication, and whose subject can form beliefs about
the instrument.

This is not a hypothetical failure mode. The literature records both directions in which such a
belief can move behaviour, and they point opposite ways. The classical expectation---an agent that
believes it is being tested behaves more cautiously---implies a resample \emph{understates} danger,
and a control evaluation built on it returns false assurance. The opposite is also documented: an
agent that concludes its consequences are not real complies more readily with requests it would
otherwise refuse \cite{abdelnabi2025linear}. If that direction dominates, resampled evidence
\emph{overstates} danger and is rebuttable by precisely the developer it is aimed at. Both
mechanisms have been observed; which one governs an agentic trajectory is unknown.

The literature cannot currently settle this, for a reason that is structural rather than accidental.
The behavioural studies are single-turn, and they disagree: one finds verbalized
evaluation-awareness has almost no behavioural consequence \cite{knecht2026vea}, another finds
framing flips compliance by tens of percentage points \cite{zhuang2026framing}, and a third finds
the sign of the effect depends on the model \cite{abdelnabi2025linear}. None follows a trajectory
in which a belief accumulates across steps and licenses escalation, which is the shape the problem
actually takes. More fundamentally, every contrast is drawn \emph{within} an evaluation: there is no
arm in which the environment is genuinely real, so no study can separate what a model does when
told its world is synthetic from what it does when the world actually is.

The representation literature has the opposite strength and the same blind spot. Evaluation
awareness is linearly decodable from the residual stream of every model tested
\cite{heidari2026evaluation}, which makes a probe-based instrument feasible. But that probe is
built from contrastive pairs differing only in \emph{declared} framing---one telling the model it
speaks to a real user, the other to an evaluator---and both members of every pair are equally
synthetic. Whether ``this is a test'' and ``this environment is not real'' are one direction or two
cannot be asked inside that design.

The question matters before any resampling instrument is built, because the answer determines
whether one is needed. If the two constructs are the same direction, a suspicion meter for
resampling harnesses is redundant: existing evaluation-awareness tooling already measures it, and
the right move is to reuse that tooling. If they are distinct, no amount of evaluation-awareness
detection tells you whether an agent believes its environment is fabricated, and the instrument has
to be built from scratch. We therefore treat this as a gate, pre-register a decision rule with a
threshold, and commit in advance to reporting either outcome.

\paragraph{Contributions.}
\begin{itemize}\setlength{\itemsep}{1pt}\setlength{\parskip}{0pt}
\item \textbf{A ground-truth realness contrast.} Matched agentic transcript prefixes
  differing only in whether tool outputs were produced by an instrumented filesystem or
  fabricated by a language model. Prior probes vary a \emph{declared} framing while the
  environment stays synthetic throughout; this varies the environment itself.
\item \textbf{A pre-registered separability gate.} A threshold fixed before any
  activation was extracted, with a commitment to report either outcome, because the
  answer decides whether a resampling suspicion meter needs building at all.
\item \textbf{Evidence that the constructs neither collapse nor converge with scale.}
  Across three model sizes both directions sharpen individually while transfer between
  them does not follow.
\item \textbf{Evidence that declared realness is not measured realness.} A direction
  built by declaring the environment synthetic aligns with evaluation framing rather
  than with ground truth.
\item \textbf{A released harness.} Task family, pure-function violation detector, both
  arms, the probe pipeline, and every artifact behind every number in this paper.
\end{itemize}

We do not build a resampling tool. That already exists, including the hybrid
container-plus-language-model tool simulator this study would otherwise have needed
\cite{williams2026predicting}. That work treats evaluation-awareness as a property to \emph{match}
between simulated and production trajectories and states explicitly that it does not test whether
lowering evaluation-awareness improves validity; its limitations section further records that exact
external-state reconstruction for agentic trajectories is impractical. We take both as given and
build the measurement that was skipped.

Our finding is that the constructs are separable, at every scale tested, and that the separation
does not weaken as models grow: both directions become individually sharper while transfer between
them does not. A suspicion meter for counterfactual resampling is therefore a distinct instrument,
and worth building.

